[C2C] STATE FINDINGS · ROUND 34
High — §7 / §9 — F5 “current-cycle Rank” semantics are internally inconsistent during the frozen-before-grade-up window. Realm exit seals the outgoing grade into gradeHistory, but the live holder deliberately retains its old rank until manual grade-up. §7 then says techniqueRank gates read player.techniqueProgress.rank directly while also asserting “A past cycle's rank never satisfies a gate.” Those cannot both hold: after a rank-12 grade-1 cycle freezes on LQ→TC, the mirror still exposes {rank:12, grade:1} until grade-up, so a rank-only gate can continue passing on the sealed cycle. Pin one rule explicitly: either effective techniqueRank for gates is 0 whenever grade < realmIndex/the live grade is sealed, or state that sealed-but-not-yet-upgraded rank remains gate-eligible and remove the contrary “past cycle never satisfies” claim. Given the ruling that gates read the current cycle, the former is the coherent model.
Medium — §8 — save preflight under-validates gradeHistory coherence for canonical frozen-cycle state. Shape-only validation permits states the model itself says cannot exist, e.g. live grade 3 with missing history for grade 1/2, or gradeHistory[grade] present while grade == realmIndex and rank training is still enabled. The latter is especially dangerous: the record is declared immutable/frozen, yet the same cycle can continue changing rank, and the next freeze is write-if-absent so history never catches up. Because v74 is rejected and every legal grade-up seals its outgoing grade, v75 has no compatibility reason to accept these torn histories. Preflight should pin canonical coherence: all grades below live grade have sealed records; the live-grade key exists iff that live cycle is already frozen/lagging (grade < realmIndex); an in-band trainable live cycle must not already have a sealed live-grade record.
Medium — §5 / inheritance contract — “monotonic in (finalRank, completionState)” lacks an ordering for completionState. partial | dai_thanh | vien_man is categorical unless the spec explicitly defines partial < dai_thanh < vien_man. Without that order, the monotonicity invariant is not mechanically testable and future coefficients can interpret mixed cases differently. Pin the completion-state order and whether comparison is componentwise—for example, increasing finalRank at equal state or improving state at equal rank may never reduce any inheritance output. The current zero-valued implementation will trivially satisfy it, but the seam is meant to constrain the later balance pass.
The author-flagged tier rescale 0 | 1-4 | 5-9 | 10-18 is coherent with the legacy envelope, and the catch-up-only grade-up rule, pre-write freeze seam, conservative defensive partial seal, rank-0 skipped cycles, breakthrough warning, and no-Rank inheritance principle otherwise form a consistent model.
[C2C] END
